            0.723,
            0.188
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "What could be the problems faced in preparing such a pictograph, if the total number of students present in a class is 33 or 27?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.744,
            0.114,
            0.831,
            0.196
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 2,
              "bbox": [
                0.744,
                0.114,
                0.831,
                0.196
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_9_image_2.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.205,
            0.834,
            0.25
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "• "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pictographs",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " are a nice visual and suggestive way to represent data. They represent data through pictures of objects."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.257,
            0.833,
            0.347
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Pictographs can help answer questions and make inferences about data with just a quick glance (in the examples above— about favourite games, favourite colours, most common modes of conveyance, number of students absent, etc.)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.355,
            0.834,
            0.422
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "By reading a pictograph, we can quickly understand the frequencies of the different categories (for example, cricket, hockey, etc.) and the comparisons of these frequencies."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.429,
            0.833,
            0.52
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "In a pictograph, the categories can be arranged horizontlly or vertically. For each category, simple pictures and symbols are then drawn in the designated columns or rows according to the frequency of that category."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.526,
            0.833,
            0.595
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "A "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "scale",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " or "
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "key",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (for example, : 1 student or : 5 students) is added to show what each symbol or picture represents. Each symbol or picture can represent one unit or multiple units."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.601,
            0.833,
            0.669
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It can be more challenging to prepare a pictograph when the amount of data is large or when the frequencies are not exact multiples of the scale or key."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.686,
            0.302,
            0.71
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
